<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="68945" href="schedule/2022/fall/PHYS/598/68945.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2022" href="schedule/2022.xml">2022</calendarYear><term id="120228" href="schedule/2022/fall.xml">Fall 2022</term><subject id="PHYS" href="schedule/2022/fall/PHYS.xml">Physics</subject><course id="598" href="schedule/2022/fall/PHYS/598.xml">Special Topics in Physics</course></parents><sectionNumber>QEN</sectionNumber><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>The course description: An introduction to quantum entanglement methods in Quantum Field Theory and gravity. Topics covered will include: entanglement in Conformal Field Theory, Renormalization Group flows, dynamical settings, topological theories and AdS/CFT. Additional topics to include black hole thermodynamics and the area law, energy conditions, the thermofield double, hawking radiation and the information paradox.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2022-08-22Z</startDate><endDate>2022-12-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LEC">Lecture</type><start>03:30 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>276</roomNumber><buildingName>Loomis Laboratory</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Faulkner" firstName="T">Faulkner, T</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>